cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the masks, please cite them as below."
title: "Polarized foregrounds in regions of the QUIJOTE-MFI wide survey: analysis code and masks"
authors:
  - family-names: "de Ferra"
    given-names: "Pablo"
    affiliation: "Departamento de Astrofísica, Universidad de La Laguna"
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24091108"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pablodeferra/Polarized-foregrounds-QUIJOTE-regions"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and sky masks of the paper "Spatial variations of polarized
  synchrotron and dust parameters from power-spectrum analysis". EE and BB
  auto- and cross-spectra of QUIJOTE-MFI, WMAP and Planck PR4 maps are measured
  with NaMaster in three Galactic cuts and four regions of the QUIJOTE-MFI wide
  survey, and a synchrotron and thermal dust model is fitted to them with a
  Wishart likelihood.
keywords:
  - cosmic microwave background
  - polarized foregrounds
  - synchrotron
  - thermal dust
  - QUIJOTE
  - power spectrum
